{
  "loreEntries": [
    {
      "loreEntryElementType": {
        "id": "01GR6AENPX6HQP8G16KNV7BNA2",
        "reference": "FLAVOR_TEXT",
        "subject": "Flavor Text"
      },
      "translations": {
        "es_ES": {
          "text": "«Uno puede sacar agua de un pozo de agua, ¿por qué no va a poder sacar melaza de un pozo de melaza? ¡No seas estúpida!».",
          "locale": "es_ES"
        },
        "de_DE": {
          "text": "„Man kann Wasser aus einem Wasserbrunnen pumpen. Also kann man doch wohl Sirup aus einem Sirupbrunnen pumpen – nicht, Dummchen?“",
          "locale": "de_DE"
        },
        "it_IT": {
          "text": "\"Come si estrae l'acqua dal pozzo, si potrà estrarre la melassa da un pozzo di melassa, credo... eh, stupida?\"",
          "locale": "it_IT"
        },
        "en_US": {
          "text": "\"You can draw water out of a water-well, so I should think you could draw treacle out of a treacle-well - eh, stupid?\"",
          "locale": "en_US"
        },
        "fr_FR": {
          "text": "« Quand il y a de l’eau dans un puits, vous savez bien comment on en tire, n’est-ce pas ? D’un puits de mélasse on s'en tire de même, comprenez-vous, petite sotte ? »",
          "locale": "fr_FR"
        }
      },
      "id": "01HPME80MN7F8B1B3XPSWJDG9X",
      "text": "\"You can draw water out of a water-well, so I should think you could draw treacle out of a treacle-well - eh, stupid?\""
    }
  ],
